 "title": "111: Info Leak Chaining",
 "desc": "Goal: Real exploits chain multiple leaks before the final payload. This exercise walks through a 3-stage leak: Step 1: format string to leak the stack canary. Step 2: format string to leak a libc address from the GOT. Step 3: compute system() address and build a ROP chain. This is how 90% of real-world exploits work.",
 "source": [
  "// Multi-stage info leak → exploit",
  "#include <stdio.h>",
  "#include <string.h>",
  "",
  "void vuln() {",
  "    char buf[32];",
  "    // Round 1: leak canary via %x",
  "    fgets(buf, 64, stdin);",
  "    printf(buf);",
  "    // Round 2: leak libc via GOT",
  "    fgets(buf, 64, stdin);",
  "    printf(buf);",
  "    // Round 3: overflow with ROP chain",
  "    fgets(buf, 64, stdin);",
  "    // stack: [buf][canary][ebp][ret]",
  "}"
 ],
